WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.080
- Hi, I'm Meaghan from Khan Academy,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.600
and in this video, we'll
walk through the reports

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.670
related to assignments on Khan Academy.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.469
After you've created
assignments on Khan Academy,

00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:17.650
and your students have
completed those assignments,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.120
you can track progress
using a variety of reports

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.120
designed to help teachers
gain a deeper understanding

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.730
of student's strengths
and areas for opportunity.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.570
Start by selecting the class
from the teacher dashboard.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.800
And then selecting scores
under the assignments tab

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.603
in the left-side navigation.

00:00:37.727 --> 00:00:40.630
This will bring you to the
assignment scores report.

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.520
In this report, you will see progress

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.440
across assignments for
all students in the class.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.310
If the assignment is a video or article,

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:50.760
and students have
completed the assignment,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.250
you will see a green check mark.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.320
To earn completion for a video,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.040
the student most have watched
at least 90% of the video

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.700
at no faster than double speed.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.900
To earn completion for an article,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.660
the student must have
clicked into the article.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.780
If the assignment is an
exercise, quiz, or test,

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.373
the student's best score will
be shown in a color-coded box.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:18.313
Boxes appear as red for scores 0-59,

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.873
yellow for scores 60-99, or
green for a score of 100.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.109
If the student has not
completed the assignment,

00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:31.253
the box will remain gray.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.300
To access a more detailed report

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.200
for an individual assignment,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.250
from the assignment scores report,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.900
select the assignment
name for any assignment

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.770
that contains questions.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.860
This includes exercises,
quizzes, and tests.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.760
This screen shows you an example

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.840
of an assignments responses report

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.330
for an exercise that
contained seven questions.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.160
On the left side, you can
select the first or last attempt

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.870
students made to answer the question.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.850
You are also able to select each question

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.093
to see students' responses.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:09.800
If you've chosen to provide

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.490
different questions for each student,

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:14.210
the questions appear in the order

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.523
students found them most challenging.

00:02:17.515 --> 00:02:19.976
The questions students incorrectly

00:02:19.976 --> 00:02:23.246
most frequently appears at the top,

00:02:23.246 --> 00:02:25.606
while the questions
students answered correctly

00:02:25.606 --> 00:02:28.910
most frequently appears at the bottom.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.180
If you've chosen to provide

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.520
the same question for all students,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.150
the questions appear in the order

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.453
in which they were presented to students.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.290
On the right side, you can
select a specific student,

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.873
or the whole class, to view the
assignment responses report.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.370
Select the responses tab on the right

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.390
to see a summary of student responses.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.510
Correct responses can be highlighted

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.763
by selecting the reveal answer button.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.820
You can view which
students gave which answers

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.200
by selecting an individual response

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.053
to display student names.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.480
Many teachers recommend
keeping students' names private

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.193
when sharing this report
with the entire class.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.430
You can select the draw tab
to reveal a scratchpad space

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:22.200
that you can use to solve the
problem live with students.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.620
Many teachers recommend using a projector

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.363
for the class to follow along.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.920
Some teachers also
suggest having a student

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.690
solve the problem step
by step for the class,

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:37.410
instead of the teacher,
as a way to encourage

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.103
student voice and build
student confidence.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.710
In the hints tab, you can view

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:46.070
the step-by-step process
to solve the problem.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:49.600
These are the same steps
provided to students in real time

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.850
when they select the "get a
hint" option in an exercise.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:57.120
You can also access the
assignment responses report

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.650
by selecting the manage tab
from the class dashboard,

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.900
and then selecting view report

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.673
for the individual assignment.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.960
The assignment scores report,

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.240
and the assignment responses report,

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.240
are helpful in monitoring assignment

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.870
progress for an entire class.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.640
If you'd like to look more closely

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.370
at the assignment progress
for a single student,

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:25.253
use the individual
student assignment report.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:29.940
From the class dashboard,
select activity overview

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.683
from the left-side navigation.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.900
Then select the individual student

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.260
whose assignment progress you want to view

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.933
by selecting the student's
name from the class list.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.623
This brings you to the
individual student report.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:48.270
Select the assignments tab to view

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.683
all assignments given to that student.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.830
This report displays
the due date and time,

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:58.100
assignment name, assignment status,

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.870
attempts made on the assignment,

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.370
and the student's best score

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.823
if the assignment is an
exercise, quiz, or test.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.790
There is also a red indicator that appears

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.610
next to the assignment status
if the assignment is late,

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:14.570
meaning the student
completed the assignment

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:15.783
after the due date.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:20.140
The individual student assignment report

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:23.043
can also be reached from the
assignment scores report.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.840
From the assignment scores report,

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.280
select the student's name
from the student list

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.620
in the assignment scores report.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:31.980
This will bring you to the student's

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.263
individual student assignment report.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:38.370
We hope this video helps
you better understand

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.660
the assignment reports on Khan Academy,

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.450
and how to best use these reports

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.913
to support student success.

